## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Window Utility Server & Launcher
#### [NEW] [src/ui/server.js](file:///c:/VOLUME%20D/AI-Powered-Bug-Pattern-Backend/src/ui/server.js)
- Lightweight, zero-dependency Node.js HTTP server (built with standard `http` module).
- Serves the frontend static files and provides local JSON API endpoints:
  - `GET /api/status`
  - `POST /api/solve`
  - `POST /api/explain`
  - `POST /api/fix`
  - `POST /api/session`
  - `POST /api/log`
  - `GET /api/config`
  - `POST /api/config`
- Reuses all existing logic in [`src/api.js`](file:///c:/VOLUME%20D/AI-Powered-Bug-Pattern-Backend/src/api.js) and [`src/config.js`](file:///c:/VOLUME%20D/AI-Powered-Bug-Pattern-Backend/src/config.js) directly (both live backend & standalone local fallback).

#### [NEW] [src/ui/launcher.js](file:///c:/VOLUME%20D/AI-Powered-Bug-Pattern-Backend/src/ui/launcher.js)
- Detects Windows Microsoft Edge and Google Chrome installations.
- Spawns the window in standalone utility mode (`--app=http://127.0.0.1:<port>`).
- Cross-platform support (fallback to `start` on Windows, `open` on macOS, `xdg-open` on Linux).

